    "result_text": "The full build passes. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a derived `ageBand` field to owners, computed from an optional `birthDate` request field against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\n**Where each piece landed** (following the existing pattern for other derived fields like `membershipLevel`/`contactPreference`):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` as an optional editable input on `OwnerFields`, and `ageBand` as a read-only derived enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) on `Owner`. These regenerate the DTOs.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter, so a value supplied at `POST` is stored and available on later `GET`s.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the owners table in all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); tests run on hsqldb.\n\n4. **`AgeBand` util** \u2014 a small single-responsibility enum holding the band boundaries (`< 18` MINOR, `18\u201364` ADULT, `\u2265 65` SENIOR) and the `of(birthDate, asOf)` computation, mirroring `MembershipLevels`.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` + a thin `ageBand(owner)` method delegating to the util. `birthDate` itself maps automatically by name in both directions, so `BuildOwner`'s existing `toOwner(...)` carries the input through with no change needed to the pipeline functions.\n\nBecause `ageBand` is derived in the mapper at response time (not stored), both the `POST` and `GET` responders return it consistently from the stored `birthDate` and effective `registrationDate`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` passes (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
